https://www.tuwien.at/en/studies/studies.requirement:
Admission to the Master's programme in 'Logic and Artificial Intelligence' is possible after completing an eligible Bachelor's degree at an accredited national or international post-secondary educational institution. In particular, a degree programme is considered eligible, provided that at least 120 ECTS credits have been completed in the subject areas of Mathematics and Computer Science, of which at least:
25 ECTS credits in mathematics and statistics, as well as the theoretical foundations of computer science, with knowledge, skills and competences acquired in accordance with the modules 'Algebra and Discrete Mathematics', 'Analysis', 'Statistics and Probability Theory', and 'Theoretical Computer Science' of the Bachelor's degree programme in Informatics at TU Wien;
20 ECTS credits in algorithms, data structures and programming, covering the knowledge, skills and competences taught in the modules 'Algorithms and Data Structures', 'Introduction to Programming' and 'Programming Paradigms' of the Bachelor's degree programme in Informatics at TU Wien.

Admission to the Master’s programme in ‘Software Engineering’ is possible after completing an eligible Bachelor’s degree at an accredited national or international post-secondary educational institution. In particular, a degree programme is considered eligible, provided that at least 120 ECTS credits have been completed in the subject areas of Mathematics and Computer Science, of which at least:
20 ECTS in mathematics and statistics, covering the knowledge, skills and competences taught in the modules ‘Algebra and Discrete Mathematics’, ‘Analysis’ and ‘Statistics and Probability Theory’ of the Bachelor’s degree programme in Informatics at TU Wien;
25 ECTS in algorithms, data structures and programming, with knowledge, skills and competences corresponding to the modules ‘Algorithms and Data Structures’, ‘Database Systems’, ‘Programming Paradigms’, ‘Introduction to Programming’ and ‘Software Engineering’ from the Bachelor’s programme in Informatics at TU Wien;
20 ECTS from the theoretical, technical and practical foundations of Computer Science, with knowledge, skills and competences corresponding to the modules ‘Computer Science Thinking’, ‘Introduction to Security’, ‘Fundamentals of Digital Systems’ and ‘Theoretical Computer Science’ of the Bachelor’s degree programme in Informatics at TU Wien.

